<!--
  BlockML Core — root Block type

  FQN: org.blockml.core.Block
  See docs/00_bom_core.md — Block and Block Instance · Fundamental Architecture Principles
       docs/02_mbml.md — Block Definition · idea · documentation
       docs/16_framework_base_types.md — Root Type Exception · Definition Branch
       docs/12_bom_object_model.md — BlockDefinition
       docs/17_type_system_bml.md — Everything is a Block
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.core"
  xmlns:bml="http://blockml.org/schema/bml">

  <idea>The universal semantic unit of BlockML — every definable concept in the grammar.</idea>

  <documentation>
    Root semantic unit of BlockML — the sole inheritance root for all Block definitions.
    Every concept in the grammar is a Block: composable domain types, ValueTypes, Languages,
    Status values, Constraints, Capabilities, Services, Libraries, and Definition meta-model
    types. Unqualified name Block resolves to org.blockml.core.Block.

    Role and constraints:
    • Sole inheritance root — omits baseType; all other definitions must declare one
    • Abstract — not used directly as a composition instance type
    • Declares no members — sub-types define their own Properties, Aggregations,
      Associations, and Capabilities via the baseType chain
    • Composition instance identity uses bml:id and bml:version (not member attributes)

    Type reference rules:
    • Any Block FQN may appear in aggregation and association member types
    • Property and Capability payload types must resolve to org.blockml.core.ValueType
    • Capability implementation type attributes must reference org.blockml.language.* FQNs

    Documentation model (on every root block definition):
    • &lt;idea&gt; — required first child; semantic meaning of the Block
    • &lt;documentation&gt; — required second child; technical description
    • Optional extensions: &lt;since&gt;, &lt;changelog&gt;, &lt;examples&gt;, &lt;references&gt;
    Omitted idea or documentation on root blocks → BML_MISSING_IDEA / BML_MISSING_DOCUMENTATION
    (warning V1).

    Serialization:
    • bml:xml ${ bml:Self } — composable instances render under their declared type tag
      (for example &lt;core:Block&gt;, &lt;myns:Wall&gt;)
    • Definition branch types (org.blockml.core.Definition and sub-types) describe block
      structure and carry their own bml:xml rules — see 19_definition_blocks_and_bml_xml.md

    Branch overview (all extend Block):
    • org.blockml.core.ValueType — property and capability payload types
    • org.blockml.core.Language — implementation language bindings
    • org.blockml.core.Status — lifecycle status references
    • org.blockml.core.Constraint — property validation constraints
    • org.blockml.core.Capability — capability implementation contracts
    • org.blockml.core.Definition — meta-model for block structure (WIP)
    • Domain bases (for example com.machineblocks.core.Block) — domain-specific branches

    See 00_bom_core.md — Block and Block Instance · 02_mbml.md — Block Definition ·
    16_framework_base_types.md — Root Type Exception · 17_type_system_bml.md.
  </documentation>
  
  <name>Block</name>
  <type>core:Block</type>
  <!-- Root block has no base type -->
  <baseType />
  
  <!-- Blocks are rendered as xml elements with the name of the block type -->
  <bml:xml>${ bml:Self }</bml:xml>
  
  <!-- Root block is abstract -->
  <abstract />
  
</block>
